{"amendments":[{"body":"Blocking: this change set does not implement the root-zone oxygenation bead described in the prompt. The actual edits only add alkalinity stoichiometry/budget plumbing and trace notes in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:6-27`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:12-23`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:366-384`, `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:224-239`, and `crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs:124-152`. None of those changes touch the substrate O2 penetration calculation, rooted-plant biomass access, guild-specific rooted contribution, or planted-vs-unplanted substrate behavior, so the acceptance criteria for deeper oxic zones, rooted-only contribution, saturation by biomass, and the 500-hour planted-substrate divergence are still unmet.","rationale":"The submitted patch is solving a different problem (nitrification alkalinity accounting) than the task under review. Even if the added code is locally correct, it cannot satisfy tanksim-6e5.5.4.3 as written."}],"summary":"I reviewed the diff inside the dirty worktree, read the changed implementation/test files, and ran targeted `cargo test -p tank_core alkalinity` plus `cargo test -p tank_core --test nitrification_alkalinity`. The alkalinity-accounting changes themselves look coherent, but the review is blocked because the patch does not implement the requested root-zone oxygenation feature from the bead prompt."}